On 13/01/18 17:28, Felipe Dengo Alvarado wrote:
> Hi, my name is Felipe, soon i will start with my master degree
> program in embedded systems, and want to focus in microelectronics
> and fpga design, so was wondering if you could give some ideas for
> the Thesis, based on what openrisc do.

Hi Felipe,

There have been some good MSc projects in the past around verification
of OpenRISC.  Do you have a preference for software or hardware side?

One possibility is to compare different approaches to verification.
There was a MSc some years ago using a UVM flow, and my group have
previously tried comparing GCC regression results for the reference
simulator (Or1ksim) with actual hardware. I don't know if anyone has
tried any sort of formal verification.

HTH,


